Z||000000||Fformula88||09-12-2001||07:01 PM||||I'd like to see what opinion would be to shutting the St. Lawrence Seaway down to international vessells.  (For those unfamiliar, it is the waterway connecting the Great Lakes with the Atlantic).<P>This waterway is a potential spot for an ecological disaster or terrorist act.  We have already seen ecological problems in the Great Lakes, like the influx of non-indigenous species like Zebra Mussels.  How they get here?  Ocean vessels clean out their bilge tanks in the lakes.<P>What would happen if a ship has taken in some water contaminated with a major disease agent... like Cholera?  It would infect the drinking water supply of all the Great Lakes region!  What if a terrorist sends in a bio-weapon on one of these boats?  With cities like Chicago, Toronto, Detriot, Cleveland, Buffalo, Windsor etc etc right on the lakes the potential for disaster is tremendous!  Railroads used to work fine transporting goods from the lakes to the coast... they can again!<P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero2m6siga.JPG">   <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000001||Wannabe||09-12-2001||08:01 PM||||It is remarkably easy to wreak untold havoc, as we saw yesterday. Unfortunately, the success of that attack may raise the bar for future terrorist attacks.||||reg||1
